 - 2026-06-07: Capstone .362 — the VERIFIER SCORECARD (finally on real data): aggregate the offline verifier proof now that the infra blockers are fixed — ACCURACY (moat scissor: MOAT_SURVIVES/SUBSUMED/INCONCLUSIVE on weak AND strong self-verify arms) + EFFICIENCY (energy-verifier vs LLM-judge: accuracy parity + cost ratio 'parity at Nx cheaper') + the cascade-router win + the ARC scaffold readiness + the facts last-retry outcome + FR-11 v25 + hardware. ANSWER the operator's 'does the verifier earn its place' question now that both energy theses are bounded-negative and the verifier is the surviving asset. paper_ready stays TRUE; frozen 0.9131 unchanged. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: capstone_v362_moatMOAT_SURVIVES_efficiencyCHEAPER_NOT_PARITY_earnsfalse_paper_ready_true_frozen_unchanged; results/experiment_3923_capstone_v362.json
 - 2026-06-07 [outer-loop planning]: Pre-staged the 2026.06.363 roadmap (10 tasks, exp3924-exp3933) + design doc (openspec/change-proposals/research-roadmap-vNEXT.md). Driver: .362 landed the offline verifier proof but its EFFICIENCY axis was invalid — the LLM-as-judge comparator scored AUROC 0.4423 (BELOW chance, gemma-4-26B 0-shot), making "CHEAPER_NOT_PARITY / earns=false" a strawman, and the cascade was degenerate (escalation_fraction=0.0). .363 makes the efficiency win CREDIBLE: diagnose+fix the judge into a competent GenRM/ThinkPRM comparator (clears chance on a separable fixture), re-run a VALID head-to-head + NON-DEGENERATE cascade (escalation>0 positive control), REPLICATE the moat on an independent held-out corpus (ProcessBench/fover_test_v4), take the first realistic ARC-AGI-3 agentic run (verifier-as-router action-efficiency vs a no-verifier baseline), retire the 4x-fabricated facts graph-grounding route, FR-11 v26 (self-learning MANDATE), clean hardware continuity (fixes the exp3922 duration_s=0.0 flag), and the hardened verifier-scorecard capstone. Added 2026-06-07 references (ProcessBench 2412.06559, ThinkPRM 2504.16828, GenRM 2408.15240, Budget-aware Discriminative Verification 2510.14913). YAML validated: parses, milestone==expected-next, exclusion-manifest lint clean (overrides present), overdue-priority lint clean. Not pushed.
 - 2026-06-07: Archive .362 -> activate .363; GREEN-GATE de-risk + RETIRE the facts graph-grounding route to honest future-work: exp3920 BLOCKED+FLAGGED a 4th consecutive time (exp3862 stub / exp3886 model-not-invoked / exp3896 separable-fixture / exp3920 blocked_llama_cpp), so add the graph-grounding fact-verifier scope to ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml (retire_if_same_verdict satisfied) and document facts as honest future-work (KGHaluBench-graded testbed for any future revival). Assert research-complete.yaml parses, the core pretest subset is green, and record the .362 below-chance-LLM-judge comparator flaw as the .363 forward-bet. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: archived_v362_v363_active_facts_retired_comparator_flaw_recorded_green_gates; results/experiment_3924_archive_v362_activate_v363_retire_facts.json
+- 2026-06-07: VALID EFFICIENCY head-to-head — energy-verifier vs the COMPETENT judge (north-star §5, finally testable; disk-reads exp3925+exp3905, no hard gate): on the exp3884 in-distribution corpus (n>=200), score with BOTH the energy ensemble (cheap CPU forward-pass) and the exp3925 competent GenRM/ThinkPRM judge (via the robust harness). POSITIVE CONTROL: assert the judge AUROC clears a defensible floor (>0.6) on THIS corpus BEFORE any verdict. Report accuracy parity/Pareto (energy within or above the judge CI) + a defensible cost ratio (wall-clock AND FLOP/token, amortized load excluded). Target: 'parity or dominance at Nx cheaper.' HONEST: if the competent judge BEATS energy on accuracy, say so — the cascade then becomes the deployable story. The 60s live-floor applies on THIS full-corpus artifact (NOT a fixture). (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=blocked_upstream_competent_judge_not_ready; results/experiment_3926_valid_efficiency_head_to_head.json
